    "field": "Climate projections",
    "problem": "Coupled climate models systematically underestimate the observed multidecadal variability of large-scale atmospheric circulation, causing future projections of extratropical climate to significantly underrepresent the true uncertainty in temperature, precipitation, and the occurrence of extreme seasons.",
    "method": "The proposed method generates synthetic climate projections by replacing the atmospheric circulation variability within a large model ensemble with surrogate variability that is statistically constrained to have the same spectral characteristics as observed circulation.",
    "task": "The task is to produce synthetic climate projections for the Northern Hemisphere extratropics by constraining climate models with observed atmospheric circulation variability to correct for underestimated internal variability and provide more realistic uncertainty ranges for future climate.",
